===Etymology 2===
{{etymon|en|id=bend}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰūgʰ-}}
From dialectal {{m|en||buck}} {{gl|"to give in, yield"; also {{m|en|bug|t=to bend}}}}, from {{bor|en|gml|bucken|t=to bend}} or {{bor|en|dum|bucken}}, {{m|dum|bocken|t=to bend}}, ultimately from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*bukkōn|t=to bend, bend repeatedly}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*bukkōną|t=to bend}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰugʰ-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*bʰewgʰ-|t=to bend}} + {{m+|gem-pro|*-ukōną|*-(u)kōną}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|bukkia|t=to bend}}. Influenced in some senses by [[#Etymology_1|buck]] “male goat” (see above). Sense “to meet, to encounter” is a {{sl|en|jam|buck|nocap=1}}.

Compare {{m|en|bow}} and {{m|en|elbow}}.

