===Noun===
{{wikidata lexeme|L3965}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q81727}}A concave [[vessel]] for drinking, usually made of opaque material (as opposed to a [[glass]]) and with a [[handle]].
#: {{cot|en|mug|pannikin}}
#: {{ux|en|Pour the tea into the '''cup'''.}}
# The contents of said vessel.
#: {{syn|en|cupful}}
#: {{ux|en|I drank two '''cups''' of water but still felt thirsty.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-22|volume=407|issue=8841|page=68|magazine=w:The Economist| title=[http://www.economist.com/news/finance-and-economics/21579860-g8-pledges-tackle-three-ts-t-time T time]| passage=In Starbucks’s case, the firm has in effect turned the process of making an expensive '''cup''' of coffee into intellectual property.}}
# A [[customary unit]] of measure
## {{lb|en|US}} A US [[unit]] of liquid measure equal to 8 [[fluid ounce]]s ({{frac|1|16}} of a US [[gallon]]; 236.5882365 [[mL]]) or 240 mL.
## {{lb|en|Canada}} A Canadian unit of measure equal to 8 imperial [[ounce]]s ({{frac|1|20}} imperial gallon; 227.3 mL) or 250 mL.
## {{lb|en|UK|dated}} A British unit of measure equal to {{frac|1|2}} imperial [[pint]] (10 imperial ounces; 284 mL) or 300 mL.
## {{lb|en|AU|NZ}} A metric unit of measure equal to 250 mL.
# {{senseid|en|Q381165}}A [[trophy]] in the shape of an oversized cup.
#: {{ux|en|The World '''Cup''' is awarded to the winner of a quadrennial football tournament.}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=5|passage=Of all the queer collections of humans outside of a crazy asylum, it seemed to me this sanitarium was the '''cup''' winner. {{...}} When you're well enough off so's you don't have to fret about anything but your heft or your diseases you begin to get queer, I suppose.}}
# A [[contest]] for which a cup is awarded.
#: {{ux|en|The World '''Cup''' is the world's most widely watched sporting event.}}
# {{lb|en|association football}} The main [[knockout]] tournament in a country, organised alongside the [[league]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=Rob Dimery; Peter Watts|title=Guinness world records|publisher=Gullane Children's Books|isbn=9780851121475
|passage=Until it was disbanded in 1999, the  European Cup-Winners Cup was contested annually by the winners of Europe&#39;s  national '''cups'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Michael Grant; Rob Robertson|title=The Management: Scotland's Great Football Bosses|publisher=Birlinn|isbn=9780857900845
|passage=Wallace had the unique distinction of being the  only player ever to play in the English, Welsh and Scottish '''Cups''' in the same  season.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Martí Perarnau|title=Pep Confidential: Inside Pep Guardiola's First Season at Bayern Munich|publisher=Birlinn|isbn=9780857908179
|passage=One week earlier, they had lost 5-2 to Borussia Dortmund in the DFB-Pokal [the German '''cup'''] final in Berlin.}}
# {{lb|en|golf}} A cup-shaped object placed in the target hole.
#: {{ux|en|The ball just misses the '''cup'''.}}
# A container in which [[dice]] are held and shaken before being thrown.
# {{lb|en|usually|_|in combination}} Any of various sweetened [[alcoholic]] [[drink]]s.
#: {{coi|en|cider '''cup'''}}, {{coi|en|gin '''cup'''}}, {{coi|en|claret '''cup'''}}
#*{{quote-book|en |year=1922 |author={{w|E.F. Benson}} |title=Miss Mapp |publisher=Heinemann |location=London |id=SBN 434 06504 8 |url=https://archive.org/details/missmappincludin0000efbe/page/142 |year_published=1970 |pages=158–159 |passage=The bridge tables were not set out in the garden-room, which entailed a scurry over damp gravel on a black, windy night, but in the little square parlour above her diningroom, where Withers, in the intervals of admitting her guests, was laying out plates of sandwiches and the chocolate cakes, reinforced when the interval for refreshments came with hot soup, whisky and syphons, and a jug of “'''cup'''” prepared according to an ancestral and economical recipe, which Miss Mapp had taken a great deal of trouble about. A single bottle of white wine, with suitable additions of ginger, nutmeg, herbs and soda-water, was the mother of a gallon of a drink that seemed aflame with fiery and probably spirituous ingredients. Guests were very careful how they partook of it, so stimulating it seemed.}}
# {{lb|en|US|Canada}} A rigid concave protective [[covering]] for the male [[genitalia]].
#: {{syn|en|box|id=protector|q1=UK}}
#: {{ux|en|Players of contact sports are advised to wear a '''cup'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|format=comic|author=Bill Amend|title=FoxTrot|url=https://www.gocomics.com/foxtrot/2000/03/27|date=Mar 27 2000|passage=Boys, I thought I told you to let the <u>store</u> tell you what '''cup''' size you needed.}}
# One of the two parts of a [[brassiere]] which each cover a [[breast]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''cups''' are made of a particularly uncomfortable material.}}
## {{n-g|Prefixed with a letter, used as a measurement of bra or breast size.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=w:Tom Clancy|title=Tom Clancy's Jack Ryan Books 1-6|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=uQurT021AuwC&pg=PT1149|page=1149
|passage="For cleavage to show up in these photos, a girl has to have '''C-cup''' breasts &mdash; at least that's what they told me once."}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} The symbol <math>\cup</math> denoting union and similar operations.
#: {{cot|en|cap}}
# {{lb|en|tarot}} A [[suit]] of the minor [[arcana]] in [[tarot]], or one of the cards from the suit.
# {{lb|en|ultimate frisbee}} A [[defense|defensive]] style characterized by a three [[player]] near [[defense]] ''cupping'' the [[thrower]]; ''or'' those three players.
# A flexible concave [[membrane]] used to temporarily attach a [[handle]] or [[hook]] to a flat surface by means of [[suction]].
#: {{syn|en|suction cup}}
